DATA_BLOCK "AGC_LOG_DB"
TITLE = 'AGC / Velocity / Trim-Diagnostic Data Logger Storage Buffer'
// v2.0 - Fuller diagnostic field set + corrected DB610 source offsets (vs v1.0):
//
//   BACKGROUND: v1.0's header comments documented DB610 source offsets
//   that predate FB610's ExpWindow input (added at v1.6). Adding
//   ExpWindow (DINT) to VAR_INPUT pushed FB610's entire VAR_OUTPUT
//   section 4 bytes later - AutoActive moved from DBX8.0 to DBX12.0,
//   Velocity_Out from DBW10 to DBW14, Lookup_PWM_Out from DBW12 to
//   DBW16, AGC_Trim_Out from DBW14 to DBW18, AGC_Out from DBB16 to
//   DBB20. Only ReferenceEstablished (DBX0.4, a VAR_INPUT bit ahead of
//   the shift) was still correct. This is the same class of bug fixed
//   in FB1111 v1.3 for DB888/FB600 - a VAR section boundary moving and
//   silently invalidating hardcoded absolute offsets downstream. All
//   offsets below are re-verified against FB610 V1.7's actual compiled
//   interface order.
//
//   NEW FIELDS (added to investigate the "AGC_Trim doesn't come back
//   down with StFlick held" symptom): FB610 v1.6 gave StNone a
//   level-driven re-clock (fires every ExpWindow encoder counts while
//   StNone AND AutoActive stay true) specifically because StNone holds
//   LEVEL rather than pulsing. StFlick was deliberately left
//   edge-triggered only (FP #FlickMem, single scan), on the stated
//   assumption that StFlick is always a genuine single-scan blip. If
//   StFlick is actually holding level in some real condition, the
//   edge-triggered step fires exactly once, FlickMem latches TRUE, and
//   AGC_Trim will not move again until StFlick drops and re-asserts -
//   which would look precisely like the reported "lock" behavior.
//   Capturing raw StNone/StFlick alongside NoneMem/FlickMem lets a
//   captured record set confirm or rule this out directly: if StFlick
//   reads TRUE across several consecutive records while FlickMem is
//   also TRUE the whole time and AGC_Trim_Out is flat, that's the
//   bug caught in the act. ExpWindow and LastTrimEncoderCount are
//   included to also rule out an ExpWindow guard/stale-zero issue on
//   the StNone side while we're in here.
//
//   NOTE: FlickMem and NoneMem are FB610 internal statics, not
//   declared VAR_OUTPUTs - but they are still real, addressable bytes
//   in DB610's instance data (same pattern FB1111 already uses to read
//   FB600 internals for DB888). No FB610 interface change is required
//   to log them.
//
//   OPEN ITEM: this DB alone does not populate itself - it still needs
//   a logging FB (FB1112, mirroring FB1111's read-and-write pattern
//   against DB610) to actually move data from DB610 into this buffer
//   every scan. FB1112 does not yet exist in the project.
//
// v1.0 - original 6-field record (AutoActive, ReferenceEstablished,
//   AGC_Out, Velocity_Out, Lookup_PWM_Out, AGC_Trim_Out). Superseded by
//   the corrected-offset, fuller-field record below.
//
// Record layout v2.0 (16 bytes, verified padding-free against FB610
// V1.7's compiled interface - all multi-byte fields land on already-
// even offsets with the field ordering below, no STRUCT auto-align
// padding traps):
//   Byte 0        : 6 status bits (AutoActive .0, ReferenceEstablished .1,
//                   StNone .2, StFlick .3, NoneMem .4, FlickMem .5)
//   Byte 1        : AGC_Out (BYTE)
//   Bytes 2-3     : Velocity_Out (INT)
//   Bytes 4-5     : Lookup_PWM_Out (INT)
//   Bytes 6-7     : AGC_Trim_Out (INT)
//   Bytes 8-11    : ExpWindow (DINT)
//   Bytes 12-15   : LastTrimEncoderCount (DINT)
//
// 600 records at 50ms/scan = 30 seconds per capture, same convention
// as DB888/LOGGING_DB. 600 x 16 bytes = 9600 bytes for the Buffer array.
//
// NOTE: confirm DB889 is actually free before compiling - if not, pick
// a different number and update both this DB's number and any
// "OPN DI 889" lines in FB1112_AGC_LOGGING (once written) to match.
//
// Source offsets below are against DB610 (MODE_SUPERVISOR / FB610
// V1.7's instance DB) as compiled - re-verify against the online DB
// Address column before wiring FB1112, per standing project discipline.
//
// COMPILE FIX: the BEGIN block below initializes ExpWindow and
// LastTrimEncoderCount (both DINT) with L#0, not plain 0 - a bare 0
// literal parses as INT and is a type mismatch against a DINT field
// initializer, which STEP7 rejects. Confirmed against DB888's own
// convention (Buffer[n].LastEncoderPulse := L#0; etc.) for its DINT
// fields. The three plain-INT fields (Velocity_Out, Lookup_PWM_Out,
// AGC_Trim_Out) correctly keep bare 0.
VERSION : 2.0


  STRUCT 	
   Index : INT  := 1;	// Active tracking write pointer (1 to 600)
   LogActive : BOOL ;	// Set to TRUE to start recording data
   LogDone : BOOL ;	// Turns TRUE automatically when buffer fills up
   Reset_Log : BOOL ;	// Pulse TRUE to clear all old log data
   Buffer : ARRAY  [1 .. 600 ] OF STRUCT 	// 30 seconds at 50ms intervals
    AutoActive : BOOL ;	// DB610.DBX 12.0
    ReferenceEstablished : BOOL ;	// DB610.DBX 0.4
    StNone : BOOL ;	// DB610.DBX 0.2 - raw classifier input, NEW v2.0
    StFlick : BOOL ;	// DB610.DBX 0.3 - raw classifier input, NEW v2.0
    NoneMem : BOOL ;	// DB610.DBX 24.1 - internal static (edge memory), NEW v2.0
    FlickMem : BOOL ;	// DB610.DBX 24.2 - internal static (edge memory), NEW v2.0
    AGC_Out : BYTE ;	// DB610.DBB 20
    Velocity_Out : INT ;	// DB610.DBW 14
    Lookup_PWM_Out : INT ;	// DB610.DBW 16
    AGC_Trim_Out : INT ;	// DB610.DBW 18
    ExpWindow : DINT ;	// DB610.DBD 8 - live reference pitch, NEW v2.0
    LastTrimEncoderCount : DINT ;	// DB610.DBD 110 - internal static, NEW v2.0
   END_STRUCT ;	
  END_STRUCT ;	
BEGIN
   Index := 1; 
   LogActive := FALSE; 
   LogDone := FALSE; 
   Reset_Log := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].AutoActive := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].ReferenceEstablished := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].StNone := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].StFlick := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].NoneMem := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].FlickMem := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].AGC_Out := B#16#0; 
   Buffer[1].Velocity_Out := 0; 
   Buffer[1].Lookup_PWM_Out := 0; 
   Buffer[1].AGC_Trim_Out := 0; 
   Buffer[1].ExpWindow := L#0; 
   Buffer[1].LastTrimEncoderCount := L#0; 
   Buffer[2].AutoActive := FALSE; 
   Buffer[2].ReferenceEstablished := FALSE; 
   Buffer[2].StNone := FALSE; 
   Buffer[2].StFlick := FALSE; 
